## Context
`agents/*.md` pin `model: standard|strong`. Profiles say reviewers sit "below
the coder tier" or are "decorrelated from the coder". Both are replaced by the
decorrelation doctrine of 1065.

## Scope
- `agents/coder.md`, `code-reviewer.md`, `prose-reviewer.md`, `gate-seat.md`,
  `adherence-seat.md`: remove the pins (per the 1063 finding on whether they
  were ever honoured).
- `profiles/{adherence-seat,gate-seat}/PROFILE.md:6-7` and
  `profiles/{code-reviewer,prose-reviewer}/PROFILE.md:6`: reword. Keep the
  pointers to `rules/workflow.md` and `rules/git.md` that
  `tests/test_agent_profiles.py:127-142` require.
- Same PR: the ROSTER model tuples (`tests/test_agent_profiles.py:32-53`) and
  the short-enum test at lines 85-93.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] No agent file or profile carries a tier pin or tier wording
- [ ] `tests/test_agent_profiles.py` edited and passes (it runs in CI, adherence marker included)
- [ ] `make check` passes
